From 5b3342ed256c4f188d1ae44914d9686469bb1c7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Dev <tonkatriathlete@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 18:30:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rep-scope GET /api/agent/events (server-side repId filter)

Close the gap where the client sends ?repId= but the server ignored it
(Case B: events carried no rep identity, nor did the linked visit).

- schema: add nullable rep_id to events (+ index on rep_id,type,created_at)
  and to visits (free-form rep id, mirrors agent_suggestions/insights)
- logEvent: accept + persist repId; forward it in the webhook envelope
- visits routes: populate the event rep from the originating visit
  (create/update/delete)
- agent events route: WHERE rep_id = ? when repId is supplied; absent => unfiltered;
  NULL rep_id never matches an explicit repId (feeds stay isolated)
- api-zod: ListEventsQueryParams gains repId; CreateVisitBody gains optional repId;
  ListEventsResponseItem columns made .nullable().optional() (payload + the other
  nullable event columns) so NULL rows no longer 500 the feed
- openapi.yaml updated as the generation source of truth
- tests: new agent-events-repid suite (rep isolation, back-compat, type+repId
  compose, write-path population, NULL-payload round-trip)

Backfill is a documented no-op: no historical rep was derivable.
